  "a library book's life is a circle. it is chosen and borrowed at the desk. it lives in a reader's house for a while - beside beds, in bags, once or twice in a garden. it comes back through the return slot. it is checked, sometimes mended with careful tape, and then reshelved in its exact place, ready to be chosen all over again": "/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/a-library-book-s-life-is-a-circle-it-is-chosen-and-borrowed-at-the-desk-37e325176b.mp3",
